 "about": "CellPilot scam-wording list. A text is NFKC-normalised and lowercased; an entry matches when every one of its terms is a substring, tried on the text as it is and again with spaces, punctuation, symbols and emoji removed. A 'medium' entry does not match when the text contains a warning marker (an anti-fraud warning quoting scam wording); a 'strong' entry does not either when the sender is an official one (an SMS gateway, a short code or a sender name), and always does from a personal number. Strong: outbound asks and counts a strike, inbound files the text as spam. Medium: outbound asks without a strike, inbound marks the text but leaves it in the inbox. Tuned for precision; see the specification.",
